  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce obligated $4.2B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Commerce recorded 8,131 awards with an average award size of $518K, and obligations are up 1.4% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show variation: FY21 was $4.5B, FY22 was $4.1B, FY23 was $5B, FY24 was $5.2B, FY25 was $4.2B, and FY26 is $4.2B. Information-technology and professional services lead spending in FY2026 to date. Other Computer Related Services is the largest NAICS category at $816M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $628M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $454M. Publishing and management consulting also appear in the top categories. The vendor list is led by REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M, with ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $134M and EARTH RESOURCES TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $111M among the next largest contractors. The top ten vendors include firms focused on IT, engineering, and mission support, with individual vendor obligations ranging from $218M to $72.4M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Department of Commerce contract spending changed over recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce reported obligations of $4.5B in FY21, $4.1B in FY22, $5B in FY23, $5.2B in FY24, $4.2B in FY25, and $4.2B in FY26 to date. The Department of Commerce shows an overall pattern of year-to-year movement, and obligations are up 1.4% year over year in the current fiscal-year-to-date totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest buying categories and who wins the work?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce spends most in technology and professional services, led by Other Computer Related Services at $816M, Computer Systems Design Services at $628M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $454M. The Department of Commerce’s top vendors include REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $134M, and EARTH RESOURCES TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $111M."
      }
    ]
